# Windows checks out with core.autocrlf by default, which rewrites every file
# to CRLF on the way to disk. Several guards in this repository read a file and
# compare it against text they hold — the citation ledger pins the exact lines a
# page cites, the command reference is regenerated and diffed, and the docs
# tests read the workflows to check a step is still there. All of them fail on
# Windows for a reason that has nothing to do with what they guard.
#
# Forcing LF is the fix rather than teaching each reader to normalise, because
# the readers are the part that keeps growing: the next guard would have to
# remember, and the failure it produces looks like a real defect.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched: byte-for-byte is the point.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
